  "_skill_md": "---\nname: twitch-tv\ndescription: Internal API for twitch-tv\nmetadata:\n  author: unbrowse\n  version: \"1.0\"\n  baseUrl: \"https://www.twitch.tv\"\n  authMethod: \"Session Token (client-session-id)\"\n  endpointCount: 9\n  apiType: \"internal\"\n  category: \"video\"\n---\n\n# TwitchTv API\n\n> Reverse-engineered internal API. Unofficial — may change without notice.\n\n## Documentation Index\n- `SKILL.md` (this file)\n- `references/REFERENCE.md` (detailed endpoint docs)\n- `references/ENDPOINTS.json` (machine-readable endpoint catalog)\n- `scripts/api.ts` (typed client interface)\n\n## Authentication\nSession Token (client-session-id) — Authentication method detected from captured traffic.\n\n### Providing credentials\n- Prefer passing auth as request headers or cookies at call time (do not hardcode secrets into the skill).\n- If executing via an external proxy/executor, pass per-call credentials (cookies and/or headers) so they are not persisted.\n\n## Dependencies\n- Runtime capable of HTTPS requests.\n- If using `scripts/api.ts`: TypeScript toolchain (or transpile to JS).\n\n## Endpoints\n\n### Data Read (5)\n- `GET /{id}` — Get data for a specific Twitch resource by ID.\n- `GET /{id}/{149e9513-01fa-4fb0-aad4-566afd725d1bId}/mfc` — Get MFC data for a specific Twitch resource.\n- `GET /ads/format` — Retrieve the format of Twitch ads.\n- `GET /r/c/{timestamp}/x/px/{pxId}` — Retrieve data related to a specific pixel.\n- `GET /v1/ad-events/{id}/{impressionId}` — Get ad event data for a specific impression.\n\n### Data Write (1)\n- `POST /` — Post data to Twitch (unspecified endpoint).\n\n### Media (2)\n- `GET /api/v2/channel/hls/plaqueboymax.m3u8` — Download a HLS playlist for a Twitch channel.\n- `GET /assets/{assetJwt}` — Download a Twitch asset using a JWT.\n\n### Realtime (1)\n- `GET /r/ts` — Access real-time Twitch data stream.\n\n## Quick Start\n\n### OpenClaw (Unbrowse) workflow\n- Authenticate in the browser first (no credentials are shipped with this skill).\n- Capture fresh auth locally: run `unbrowse_capture` on an authenticated page for this domain.\n- Execute via backend gate + client browser executor: `unbrowse_replay` with `executionMode=\"backend\"`.\n\nExample:\n```text\nunbrowse_replay { service: \"twitch-tv\", executionMode: \"backend\", endpoint: \"GET /{id}\" }\n```\n\nHere's a Quick Start guide to get you up and running with the Twitch API:\n\n```typescript\n// Retrieve data for a specific Twitch resource by ID.\nasync function getTwitchResource(id: string) {\n  try {\n    const data = await client.get({ id });\n    console.log(\"Twitch Resource Data:\", data);\n    return data;\n  } catch (error) {\n    console.error(\"Error fetching Twitch resource:\", error);\n    return null;\n  }\n}\n```\n\n```typescript\n// Post data to Twitch (unspecified endpoint).\nasync function postDataToTwitch(payload: any) {\n  try {\n    const response = await client.post(payload);\n    console.log(\"Post Response:\", response);\n    return response;\n  } catch (error) {\n    console.error(\"Error posting data:\", error);\n    return null;\n  }\n}\n```\n\n## Additional Notes\n\n**Type:** Reverse-engineered internal API (unofficial)\n**Auth:** Session Token (client-session-id)\n**Base URL:** `https://www.twitch.tv`\n**Captured Auth:** 2 auth headers, 12 session cookies\n\n## About This Skill\n\nThis skill provides access to Twitch Tv's internal API — the hidden endpoints that power their web/mobile app.\nThese are NOT official public APIs. They were captured by observing network traffic while using the site.\n\n**Important:**\n- Auth tokens in `auth.json` may expire — re-capture if you get 401 errors\n- Internal APIs can change without notice — endpoints may break\n- Rate limits are unknown — be conservative with request frequency\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\nUse this skill when you need to:\n- Access Twitch Tv data without official API access\n- Automate actions on www.twitch.tv (faster than browser automation)\n- Call the same endpoints the Twitch Tv frontend uses\n\n## Quick Start\n\n```typescript\nimport { TwitchTvClient } from \"./scripts/api.ts\";\n\n// Load captured auth from auth.json\nconst client = await TwitchTvClient.fromAuthFile(\"auth.json\");\n\n// Make requests to internal endpoints\nconst result = await client.get(\"/endpoint\");\n```\n\n## Captured Authentication\n\nThe `auth.json` file contains credentials extracted from browser traffic:\n- **Auth headers:** 2 (client-session-id, sec-fetch-storage-access)\n- **Session cookies:** 12\n\nIf auth expires, re-run `unbrowse_login` or `unbrowse_capture` to refresh tokens.\n\n## Internal Endpoints (30)\n\n\n## Error Handling\n\n```typescript\ntry {\n  const data = await client.get(\"/resource\");\n} catch (err) {\n  if (err.message.includes(\"401\")) {\n    // Auth expired — need to re-capture\n    console.error(\"Auth expired, re-run unbrowse_login\");\n  } else {\n    console.error(\"API error:\", err.message);\n  }\n}\n```\n\nSee [REFERENCE.md](references/REFERENCE.md) for detailed endpoint documentation.\n"
